Title:
Armory (armory-rs) — Rust Beacon Object Files (BOFs) collection for Cobalt Strike

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Armory is an archived repository containing a large catalog of Cobalt Strike-compatible BOFs implemented in Rust (COFF object files). It provides post-exploitation capabilities across situational awareness, remote operations, Active Directory/Entra ID tradecraft, Kerberos abuse (Rubeus-like functionality), and multiple process injection techniques. A notable component is a BYOVD-oriented “kernel BOF” framework intended to manipulate kernel/VTL0 state (e.g., removing kernel callbacks, disabling ETW Threat Intelligence, bypassing PPL, toggling WDigest caching, token swapping, and credential dumping from VTL0 LSASS even with Credential Guard—while acknowledging VTL1 secrets remain protected). The repo emphasizes operational constraints and documentation per BOF (argument order, build commands, example usage, output shape, and YARA rules). It’s primarily useful for red teams/pentesters and security researchers building or emulating Cobalt Strike tradecraft, and for defenders analyzing BOF behaviors and writing detections. Interesting due to the breadth of Windows-native API usage, Rust-based BOF engineering, and inclusion of kernel/BYOVD tradecraft patterns.

Technical Focus:
- Rust-based BOF/COFF development for Cobalt Strike (Beacon packed-argument ABI)
- Windows API/NTAPI tradecraft (NetAPI32, LSA, WTS, LDAP, RPC, COM, WMI, ETW)
- Kerberos offensive operations (AS-REQ/TGS-REQ, S4U, roasting, PTT, ticket extraction)
- Process injection primitives (CreateRemoteThread, NtCreateThreadEx, APC, thread hijack, PEB KernelCallbackTable)
- AD CS / certificate services enumeration and abuse workflows
- BYOVD-style kernel manipulation concepts (callbacks, PPL, ETW TI, DSE cycles, Credential Guard boundaries)

Use Cases:
- Build and run BOFs for host/network situational awareness from Cobalt Strike
- Execute AD/Entra ID discovery and credential/token collection (e.g., Token Broker cache, WAM token requests)
- Perform Kerberos ticket operations (roasting, S4U delegation abuse, ticket triage/dump/PTT)
- Conduct remote admin actions (service/task/registry operations, firewall rule changes, process handle manipulation)
- Research/detect BOF behaviors using provided per-BOF YARA rules and documented IOCs/outputs
- Prototype or emulate kernel/BYOVD post-exploitation techniques in controlled labs

Keywords:
Cobalt Strike, BOF, Beacon Object File, COFF, Rust, rustbof, boflink, Windows API, NTAPI, LsaCallAuthenticationPackage, Kerberos, AS-REQ, TGS-REQ, S4U2Self, S4U2Proxy, Pass-the-Ticket, LDAP, AD CS, Entra ID, Azure AD, WAM, Token Broker, DPAPI, BYOVD, PPL bypass, ETW Threat Intelligence, DSE, Credential Guard, LSASS dumping, process injection, NtQuerySystemInformation, MiniDumpWriteDump, EFSRPC, PetitPotam, CVE-2022-26923